:pack   Treasure Trash — the teaching rooms
:format 1
;
;  legend  # wall  - floor  @ raccoon  $ bag  C full can  c empty can  x spilled trash
;          B recycle bin (full)  b recycle bin (empty)  s sponge  d cardboard
;          w wheelie bin (empty)  F couch  Y bicycle  U rug  E exit
;          a multi-cell piece is a touching blob of one letter
;          terrain rides in :water — ~ canal  = filled in  % grease  O grate  * glass  _ covered
;
;  Chapter 1 is the verbs, chapter 2 the containers, chapter 3 the floor,
;  chapter 4 the rollers, chapter 5 the bodies.
;  Every room declares a :gate — what covers its lesson, and what verify.mjs takes away
;  to prove the exit will not open without it.
;

:level  T1
:name   Doorway
:teach  the exit
:gate   none
:par    3
:traps  0
:solves 1
:solve  rrr
:note   No bags, so the exit is live from the first move; the lesson is reaching it.
:grid
#####
#@--E
#####
:end

:level  T2
:name   Held Up
:teach  the exit waits on the bags
:gate   kind tear
:arm    on
:par    3
:traps  0
:solves 1
:solve  D!ur
:note   The exit is one step away and does nothing while the bag is out.
:grid
#####
#-@E#
#-$-#
#---#
#####
:end

:level  T3
:name   Shove
:teach  a push moves one thing one cell
:gate   kind push
:arm    on
:par    4
:traps  0
:solves 1
:solve  RRdd
:note   The can stands in the only corridor and is shoved past the turning, not out of it.
:grid
#######
#@c---#
###-###
###E###
#######
:end

:level  T4
:name   No Room
:teach  a shove needs somewhere for the thing to go
:gate   kind push
:arm    on
:par    4
:traps  0
:solves 2
:solve  ldRd
:note   The can is in the mouth of the exit alcove; shoving it onto the exit is refused.
:grid
#######
#--@--#
#--c--#
#-#E#-#
#-###-#
#-----#
#######
:end

:level  T5
:name   The Fan
:teach  the trash lands away from you, and it stays
:gate   kind tear
:arm    on
:par    5
:traps  0
:solves 1
:solve  ruL!ru
:note   Struck from below or from the left the fan would reach the exit, and the strike is refused.
:grid
#######
#---E-#
#--$--#
#--@--#
#-----#
#######
:end

:level  T6
:name   Take It Back
:teach  undo and restart
:gate   none
:arm    on
:par    3
:traps  4
:solves 1
:solve  U!dd
:note   Four of the strikes here bury the way out, and none of them costs more than one undo.
:grid
#######
#-----#
#--$--#
#-c@--#
#--E--#
#######
:end

:level  T7
:name   Set Down
:teach  the full can, and the bag it puts down
:gate   kind push
:arm    on
:par    7
:traps  2
:solves 1
:solve  RurDR!lu
:note   The bag lands beside the can, and the can is then in every fan, so it is shoved clear
:grid
#######
#--E--#
#@C---#
#-----#
#-----#
#######
:end

:level  T8
:name   Spent
:teach  a spent can is not something the exit waits for
:gate   kind tear
:arm    on
:par    3
:traps  2
:solves 1
:solve  R!lu
:note   The can is still standing when the door opens, which is the whole of the lesson.
:grid
#######
#E----#
#@$-c-#
#-----#
#-----#
#######
:end

:level  T9
:name   Recycling
:teach  the recycle bin, and the trash it sheds
:gate   kind push
:arm    on
:par    2
:traps  0
:solves 1
:solve  Ru
:note   One shove clears the yard, and nothing is torn.
:grid
#######
#-E---#
#@B---#
#-----#
#-----#
#######
:end

:level  T10
:name   Nowhere To Put It
:teach  a container needs room for what it puts down
:gate   kind push
:arm    on
:par    4
:traps  0
:solves 1
:solve  urDu
:note   The room before this one with one wall added, and the shove that solved it refused.
:grid
#######
#-E---#
#@B-#-#
#-----#
#-----#
#######
:end

:level  T11
:name   Bridged
:teach  trash fills a canal, and the crossing is permanent
:gate   erase 2,1
:arm    on
:par    8
:traps  0
:solves 1
:solve  RRRRdrru
:note   The bin sheds into the water rather than onto the floor, and what it sheds is the bridge.
:grid
#########
#@B----E#
#-------#
#########
:end
